description: For scalar programs the self-compiled compiler's output is byte-identical to native's (P12.4/P12.5). For eval-heavy programs the two emit different text with the same results, so the compiler is not yet its own fixed point. Find the ordering source (gensym or warm-order, see STATUS P8.0) and close it, or record it as a named limit of the self-hosting claim.
